import json, statistics, html
from pathlib import Path

root = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / 'audit/performance'
def read(path):
    return json.loads((root / path).read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig'))
def median_rows(phase):
    groups = {}
    for suffix in ['', '-repeat1', '-repeat2']:
        for row in read(phase + suffix + '/lighthouse-summary.json')['rows']:
            groups.setdefault((row['path'], row['mode']), []).append(row)
    return {key: {**rows[0], **{field: statistics.median(r[field] for r in rows) for field in ['score','lcp','fcp','tbt','cls','speedIndex','bytes']}, 'runs':len(rows)} for key, rows in groups.items()}
before, after = median_rows('before'), median_rows('after')
comparison = [{'path': key[0], 'mode':key[1], 'before':row, 'after':after[key]} for key,row in before.items()]
(root/'comparison.json').write_text(json.dumps(comparison, indent=2), encoding='utf-8')
esc = html.escape
rows = ''.join(f'<tr><td>{esc(r["path"])}<br>{r["mode"]}</td><td>{r["before"]["runs"]}</td><td>{r["before"]["score"]:g} → {r["after"]["score"]:g}</td><td>{r["before"]["lcp"]/1000:.2f} → {r["after"]["lcp"]/1000:.2f}</td><td>{r["before"]["tbt"]:g} → {r["after"]["tbt"]:g}</td><td>{r["before"]["cls"]:.3f} → {r["after"]["cls"]:.3f}</td><td>{r["before"]["bytes"]/1024:.0f} → {r["after"]["bytes"]/1024:.0f}</td></tr>' for r in comparison)
browsers = {p:read(p+'/browser-metrics.json')['rows'] for p in ['before','after']}
jsrows = ''.join(f'<tr><td>{esc(b["path"])}</td><td>{b["jsBytes"]/1024:.1f}</td><td>{a["jsBytes"]/1024:.1f}</td></tr>' for b,a in zip(browsers['before'],browsers['after']) if b['mode']=='desktop')
checks = []
for file in ['functional-results.json','cache-verification.json']:
    data=read(file); results=data['results']
    checks.append(f'<li><a href="{file}">{file}</a>: {sum(r["status"]=="PASS" for r in results)}/{len(results)} passed.</li>')
report = '''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>OM Food performance audit</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;color:#183c2c;background:#faf5e9;max-width:1180px;margin:40px auto;padding:24px}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:42px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:white;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:12px;text-align:left;border:1px solid #ddd}th{background:#183c2c;color:white}a{color:#984f32}.note{padding:20px;background:#eee4cf}li{margin:8px 0}</style><h1>OM Food and Spices LLP<br>Performance audit and deployed improvements</h1><p>18 November 2026 · Branch <code>codex/performance-2026-11-18</code></p><p><a href="https://om-food-exact-preview.vercel.app">Live website</a> · Production deployment <code>dpl_3j5Xeur9oizKxn2UAPZzrD2EoeQp</code>: Ready.</p>
<h2>Measured outcome</h2><ul><li>Mobile blog transfer: median 915,036 → 410,868 bytes, about 55% less.</li><li>Homepage mobile Lighthouse score: median 97 → 97. LCP approximately 2.49 → 2.48 seconds: essentially unchanged.</li><li>Initial desktop JavaScript fell across sampled routes. Exact five-second samples appear below.</li><li>Lab enquiry click-to-paint proxy: 258 → 113 ms. First usable form: 399 → 611 ms, a 212 ms first-open cost from loading the form on demand.</li><li>Five-second animation sample: frames exceeding 50 ms fell from 7 to 0. This is headless Chromium cadence, not proof of physical-device FPS.</li></ul>
<h2>Implemented changes and reasons</h2><ul><li>Hero keeps three virtual image panels instead of the entire catalogue in a wide strip. Seamless horizontal wrap and 2,250 ms autoplay remain.</li><li>Hero/gallery timers stop offscreen, in hidden tabs, and with reduced-motion preference. Below-fold galleries no longer get priority image loading.</li><li>Hindi/Gujarati dictionaries load when selected. English no longer performs repeated whole-page mutation scans; translation avoids observing its own edits.</li><li>Enquiry form and individual admin managers load on demand. This reduces initial JavaScript with the documented first-form tradeoff above.</li><li>Blog cards receive summaries instead of complete article bodies. Detail pages retrieve a single published article; related product articles retrieve only three small links.</li><li>Public cached queries select published content only. Auth checks deduplicate within a server request through React cache, never across users or requests.</li><li>Responsive image sizes prevent oversized blog/logo downloads. Footer logos are not prioritized. Bulk product/blog card prefetch is disabled.</li><li>Original photos, theme, layout, fonts, product data, WhatsApp destinations and hero copy were preserved. No new project dependency or database migration was added.</li></ul>
<h2>Lighthouse before → after</h2><p>Home and blog use medians of three runs per device profile; other routes have one run and are less conclusive. Lighthouse 13.6.0, Chrome, mobile simulated throttling. Transfer is total Lighthouse network bytes, not uncompressed asset size. TBT did not consistently improve.</p><table><tr><th>Route / profile</th><th>Runs per phase</th><th>Score</th><th>LCP seconds</th><th>TBT ms</th><th>CLS</th><th>Transfer KiB</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table>
<h2>Initial JavaScript: desktop browser samples</h2><p>Cold contexts; five seconds after DOMContentLoaded. Includes authenticated dashboard. These are bounded-window samples, not complete-transfer guarantees; timing and cache variance can affect individual results.</p><table><tr><th>Route</th><th>Before KiB</th><th>After KiB</th></tr>'''+jsrows+'''</table>
<h2>Functional, privacy and content verification</h2><ul>'''+''.join(checks)+'''<li>All 12 public articles, original titles, dates, links and images rechecked after deployment: <a href="../blog/all-12-public-results.json">article evidence</a>.</li><li>Tested hero autoplay and wrap, reduced motion, offscreen suspension, language refresh/restoration, modal, filters, gallery, mobile navigation, widths 390/768/1440 and authenticated admin sections.</li><li>Temporary SEO marker appeared in a fresh anonymous session, then exact original was restored. Temporary draft was visible only in authorized preview, absent from public payload, then deleted. Logout invalidated access.</li><li>Counts after audit: products 10, categories 2, blogs 12, enquiries 1, media 0. Audit log entries retained. No customer enquiry or message was sent.</li><li>Lint, production build and relevant blog/date/enquiry validation checks passed. Local production and deployed functional checks passed.</li></ul>
<h2>Visual evidence</h2><p>Original and optimized screenshots retained for desktop and mobile home, blog and product. Mean absolute RGB channel differences ranged 0.28–1.01 on a 0–255 scale; this is not a claim of pixel identity.</p><ul><li><a href="before/visual/home-390.png">Before mobile home</a> / <a href="after-local/visual/home-390.png">Optimized mobile home</a></li><li><a href="before/visual/blog-1440.png">Before desktop blog</a> / <a href="after-local/visual/blog-1440.png">Optimized desktop blog</a></li></ul>
<h2>Limits and remaining work</h2><div class="note">Google PageSpeed Insights API returned HTTP 429 (quota exhausted), so no cloud PSI or field Core Web Vitals claim is made. Lighthouse is laboratory data; true field INP and 28-day CWV require traffic/CrUX or RUM. No physical iPhone/Android or Safari engine was available. Timings vary with network and cold starts; single-run dashboard improvements are not causal proof. Consider real-device checks and field monitoring next. First enquiry-open chunk delay remains an explicit tradeoff.</div>
<h2>Kept simple</h2><p>Existing Manrope WOFF2, WebP/AVIF image pipeline, native CSS transforms and observers already fit the task. No animation library, font replacement, destructive image recompression, speculative index, or cache of authenticated private data was added. Existing database indexes suit the small dataset; EXPLAIN round-trip time includes network latency and is not SQL CPU time.</p>
<h2>Raw evidence and methodology</h2><p><a href="comparison.json">Comparison JSON</a> · <a href="before/lighthouse-summary.json">Before Lighthouse</a> · <a href="after/lighthouse-summary.json">After Lighthouse</a> · <a href="before/interaction.json">Before interaction</a> · <a href="after/interaction.json">After interaction</a> · <a href="database-audit-after.json">Database audit</a> · <a href="pagespeed-insights.json">PSI response</a>. Repeated reports live in before-repeat1/2 and after-repeat1/2; individual Lighthouse reports include requests and diagnostics.</p><p>References: <a href="https://nextjs.org/docs/15/app/api-reference/components/image">Next Image responsive sizes</a>, <a href="https://react.dev/reference/react/cache">React request-local cache</a>, <a href="https://web.dev/articles/lab-and-field-data-differences">Lab versus field measurements</a>.</p></html>'''
(root/'PERFORMANCE-REPORT.html').write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
print('Report written; comparison rows:',len(comparison))
